  "summary_en": "This is the Croatian machine-translated version of the European Commission's policy page explaining the EU AI Act (Regulation 2024/1689). It covers the four risk tiers, the nine prohibited practices, high-risk uses and obligations, the AI Pact, and the application timeline as amended by the Digital Omnibus. Robots come up only once, as an example: AI in robot-assisted surgery is a high-risk product safety component.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "The AI Act sets four risk levels: unacceptable, high, limited and minimal.",
   "Nine AI practices are prohibited, including social scoring and real-time remote biometric identification for law enforcement in public spaces.",
   "High-risk uses include AI safety components in products, such as robot-assisted surgery, and AI in critical infrastructure such as transport.",
   "High-risk obligations in Annex III areas apply from 2 December 2027; for products covered by Annex I, the transition period runs to 2 August 2028.",
   "The voluntary AI Pact and the AI Act Service Desk support implementation."
